IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa25-notices-courts.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 37, "Notice of appointment of certain
-- officers" and "Courts and legal proceedings": ss 1154 to 1157 (lines 16410-16445 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of: silent, list not closed,
--               includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every name below begins with the section label it implements.
--
-- Finding (NOTES.md): s 1154(1)(b) names an interim manager under s 76 of the Charities Act 2011 only, but s 1154(2)(b)
-- also names an interim manager under s 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008, and (2)(bb) a receiver or manager
-- under that section: the duty of subsection (1) does not list the Northern Ireland appointments that subsection (2) says
-- who gives notice of. The duty function answers NOTHING for them (fork F9).

§ `Part 37: companies, supplementary provisions`

§§ `Notice of appointment of certain officers`

DECLARE `s 1154 appointment` IS ONE OF
    `s 1154 a judicial factor appointed in relation to a company (in Scotland)`
    `s 1154 an interim manager appointed in relation to a company under s 76 of the Charities Act 2011`
    `s 1154 an interim manager appointed in relation to a company under s 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008`
    `s 1154 a receiver or manager appointed in relation to a company under s 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008`
    `s 1154 a manager appointed in relation to a company under s 47 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004`
    `s 1154 another appointment in relation to a company`

DECLARE `s 1154 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 1154 the judicial factor`
    `s 1154 the Charity Commission`
    `s 1154 the Charity Commission for Northern Ireland`
    `s 1154 the Regulator of Community Interest Companies`

DECLARE `s 1154 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1154 give notice of the appointment to the registrar`
    `s 1154 give notice of the termination of the appointment to the registrar`

-- src:16411 | 1154 Duty to notify registrar of certain appointments etc
-- src:16412 | (1) Notice must be given to the registrar of the appointment in relation to a company of—
-- src:16413 | (a) a judicial factor (in Scotland),
-- src:16414 | (b) an interim manager appointed under section 76 of the Charities Act 2011, or
-- src:16415 | (c) a manager appointed under section 47 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (c. 27).
@ref s 1154(1) Notice must be given to the registrar of the appointment (src:16411-16415)
GIVEN appointment IS A `s 1154 appointment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1154(1) notice of the appointment must be given to the registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER appointment
    WHEN `s 1154 a judicial factor appointed in relation to a company (in Scotland)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1154 an interim manager appointed in relation to a company under s 76 of the Charities Act 2011` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1154 a manager appointed in relation to a company under s 47 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1154 an interim manager appointed in relation to a company under s 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1)(b) names s 76 of the Charities Act 2011 only, though subsection (2)(b) names this appointment (fork F9)
    WHEN `s 1154 a receiver or manager appointed in relation to a company under s 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1) does not list this appointment, though subsection (2)(bb) names it (fork F9)
    WHEN `s 1154 another appointment in relation to a company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (1) lists three appointments without "only"

-- src:16416 | (2) The notice must be given—
-- src:16417 | (a) in the case of appointment of a judicial factor, by the judicial factor;
-- src:16418 | (b) in the case of appointment of an interim manager under section 76 of the Charities Act 2011or section 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008 , by the Charity Commission;
-- src:16419 | (bb) in the case of appointment of a receiver or manager under section 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008, by the Charity Commission for Northern Ireland;
-- src:16420 | (c) in the case of appointment of a manager under section 47 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004, by the Regulator of Community Interest Companies.
@ref s 1154(2) Who gives the notice (src:16416-16420)
GIVEN appointment IS A `s 1154 appointment`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1154 party`
`s 1154(2) the person who must give the notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER appointment
    WHEN `s 1154 a judicial factor appointed in relation to a company (in Scotland)` THEN JUST `s 1154 the judicial factor`
    WHEN `s 1154 an interim manager appointed in relation to a company under s 76 of the Charities Act 2011` THEN JUST `s 1154 the Charity Commission`
    WHEN `s 1154 an interim manager appointed in relation to a company under s 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008` THEN JUST `s 1154 the Charity Commission`
    WHEN `s 1154 a receiver or manager appointed in relation to a company under s 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008` THEN JUST `s 1154 the Charity Commission for Northern Ireland`
    WHEN `s 1154 a manager appointed in relation to a company under s 47 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` THEN JUST `s 1154 the Regulator of Community Interest Companies`
    WHEN `s 1154 another appointment in relation to a company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (2) names the giver of the notice for five appointments without "only"

-- src:16421 | (3) The notice must specify an address at which service of documents (including legal process) may be effected on the person appointed.
@ref s 1154(3) The notice must specify an address for service (src:16421)
GIVEN `the notice specifies an address at which service of documents (including legal process) may be effected on the person appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1154(3) the notice meets the requirement as to the address for service` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies an address at which service of documents (including legal process) may be effected on the person appointed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must specify an address at which service of documents (including legal process) may be effected on the person appointed" (a bare "must" not met: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- src:16422 | Notice of a change in the address for service may be given to the registrar by the person appointed.
@ref s 1154(3) Notice of a change in the address for service (src:16422)
GIVEN `the person giving the notice is the person appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1154(3) the person may give the registrar notice of a change in the address for service` MEANS
    IF `the person giving the notice is the person appointed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Notice of a change in the address for service may be given to the registrar by the person appointed"

-- src:16423 | (4) Where notice has been given under this section of the appointment of a person, notice must also be given to the registrar of the termination of the appointment.
-- src:16424 | This notice must be given by the person specified in subsection (2).
@ref s 1154(4) Notice of the termination of the appointment (src:16423-16424)
GIVEN `notice has been given under this section of the appointment of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1154(4) notice of the termination of the appointment must be given to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `notice has been given under this section of the appointment of the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where notice has been given under this section of the appointment of a person, notice must also be given to the registrar of the termination of the appointment" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16411 | 1154 Duty to notify registrar of certain appointments etc
-- src:16412 | (1) Notice must be given to the registrar of the appointment in relation to a company of—
-- src:16413 | (a) a judicial factor (in Scotland),
-- src:16414 | (b) an interim manager appointed under section 76 of the Charities Act 2011, or
-- src:16415 | (c) a manager appointed under section 47 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (c. 27).
-- src:16416 | (2) The notice must be given—
-- src:16417 | (a) in the case of appointment of a judicial factor, by the judicial factor;
-- src:16418 | (b) in the case of appointment of an interim manager under section 76 of the Charities Act 2011or section 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008 , by the Charity Commission;
-- src:16419 | (bb) in the case of appointment of a receiver or manager under section 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008, by the Charity Commission for Northern Ireland;
-- src:16420 | (c) in the case of appointment of a manager under section 47 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004, by the Regulator of Community Interest Companies.
-- src:16421 | (3) The notice must specify an address at which service of documents (including legal process) may be effected on the person appointed.
-- src:16422 | Notice of a change in the address for service may be given to the registrar by the person appointed.
-- src:16423 | (4) Where notice has been given under this section of the appointment of a person, notice must also be given to the registrar of the termination of the appointment.
-- src:16424 | This notice must be given by the person specified in subsection (2).
@ref s 1154 Duty to notify registrar of certain appointments etc (the duty as a regulative rule: no time limit is stated in this section) (src:16411-16424)
GIVEN giver IS A `s 1154 party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 1154 party` `s 1154 act`
`s 1154(1) the person specified in subsection (2) must give the registrar notice of the appointment` MEANS
    PARTY giver
    MUST `s 1154 give notice of the appointment to the registrar`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY giver BECAUSE "s 1154(1): notice of the appointment was not given to the registrar"

-- ---- s 1155: Offence of failure to give notice -------------------------------------------------------------
-- "within the period of 14 days after the appointment": the period begins on the day after the appointment, so the
-- last day is the day of the appointment plus 14 days (fork F3: the other reading counts the day of appointment as day 1).

-- src:16425 | 1155 Offence of failure to give notice
-- src:16426 | (1) If a judicial factor fails to give notice of his appointment in accordance with section 1154 within the period of 14 days after the appointment he commits an offence.
@ref s 1155(1) Offence: a judicial factor fails to give notice within 14 days (src:16425-16426)
GIVEN `the date of the appointment` IS A DATE
      `the date on which notice was given to the registrar in accordance with s 1154` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1155(1) the judicial factor commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which notice was given to the registrar in accordance with s 1154`
    WHEN JUST given THEN
        IF given AT MOST (`the date of the appointment` PLUS 14)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a judicial factor fails to give notice of his appointment in accordance with section 1154 within the period of 14 days after the appointment he commits an offence" (an "if" that is not met: notice was given in time)
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN (`the date of the appointment` PLUS 14)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 14 days have not yet run out, so the failure is not yet made out

-- src:16427 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1155(2) Penalty for an offence under s 1155 (src:16427)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1155(2) the penalty for an offence under s 1155` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- The judicial factor's duty with its 14 days, as a regulative rule: the failure to act in time is the offence of s 1155(1).
-- src:16425 | 1155 Offence of failure to give notice
-- src:16426 | (1) If a judicial factor fails to give notice of his appointment in accordance with section 1154 within the period of 14 days after the appointment he commits an offence.
@ref s 1155(1) Offence: a judicial factor fails to give notice within 14 days (src:16425-16426)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 1154 party` `s 1154 act`
`s 1155(1) the judicial factor must give the registrar notice within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1154 the judicial factor`
    MUST `s 1154 give notice of the appointment to the registrar`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1154 the judicial factor` BECAUSE "s 1155(1): notice of the appointment was not given within the period of 14 days after the appointment (an offence)"

§§ `Courts and legal proceedings`

-- ---- s 1156: Meaning of "the court" ---------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1156 court` IS ONE OF
    `s 1156 the High Court in England and Wales`
    `s 1156 the county court`
    `s 1156 the Court of Session`
    `s 1156 the sheriff court`
    `s 1156 the High Court in Northern Ireland`

-- src:16429 | 1156 Meaning of “the court”
-- src:16430 | (1) Except as otherwise provided, in the Companies Acts “the court” means—
-- src:16431 | (a) in England and Wales, the High Court or the county court;
-- src:16432 | (b) in Scotland, the Court of Session or the sheriff court;
-- src:16433 | (c) in Northern Ireland, the High Court.
@ref s 1156(1) Meaning of "the court" (src:16429-16433)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 1156 court`
`s 1156(1) the courts that are "the court" in the part of the United Kingdom` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN LIST `s 1156 the High Court in England and Wales`, `s 1156 the county court`
    WHEN Scotland THEN LIST `s 1156 the Court of Session`, `s 1156 the sheriff court`
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN LIST `s 1156 the High Court in Northern Ireland`

-- src:16429 | 1156 Meaning of “the court”
-- src:16430 | (1) Except as otherwise provided, in the Companies Acts “the court” means—
-- src:16431 | (a) in England and Wales, the High Court or the county court;
-- src:16432 | (b) in Scotland, the Court of Session or the sheriff court;
-- src:16433 | (c) in Northern Ireland, the High Court.
@ref s 1156(1) Meaning of "the court" (src:16429-16433)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      tribunal IS A `s 1156 court`
      `it is otherwise provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1156(1) the tribunal is the court` MEANS
    IF `it is otherwise provided`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except as otherwise provided": the provision that provides otherwise decides (an "except" once met: fork F6)
    ELSE IF elem tribunal (`s 1156(1) the courts that are "the court" in the part of the United Kingdom` place)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the Companies Acts “the court” means— (a) in England and Wales, the High Court or the county court; (b) in Scotland, the Court of Session or the sheriff court; (c) in Northern Ireland, the High Court"

-- src:16434 | (2) The provisions of the Companies Acts conferring jurisdiction on “the court” as defined above have effect subject to any enactment or rule of law relating to the allocation of jurisdiction or distribution of business between courts in any part of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 1156(2) The jurisdiction conferred on "the court" is subject to allocation of jurisdiction (src:16434)
GIVEN `an enactment or rule of law relating to the allocation of jurisdiction or distribution of business between courts applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1156(2) the jurisdiction conferred on the court yields to the allocation of jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `an enactment or rule of law relating to the allocation of jurisdiction or distribution of business between courts applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "have effect subject to any enactment or rule of law relating to the allocation of jurisdiction or distribution of business between courts"

-- ---- s 1157: Power of court to grant relief in certain cases ----------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1157 defendant` IS ONE OF
    `s 1157 an officer of a company`
    `s 1157 a person employed by a company as auditor (whether or not an officer of the company)`
    `s 1157 another person`

-- src:16437 | 1157 Power of court to grant relief in certain cases
-- src:16438 | (1) If in proceedings for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust against—
-- src:16439 | (a) an officer of a company, or
-- src:16440 | (b) a person employed by a company as auditor (whether he is or is not an officer of the company),
-- src:16441 | it appears to the court hearing the case that the officer or person is or may be liable but that he acted honestly and reasonably, and that having regard to all the circumstances of the case (including those connected with his appointment) he ought fairly to be excused, the court may relieve him, either wholly or in part, from his liability on such terms as it thinks fit.
@ref s 1157(1) The court's power to relieve an officer or auditor from liability (src:16437-16441)
GIVEN defendant IS A `s 1157 defendant`
      `the proceedings are for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the defendant is or may be liable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the defendant acted honestly and reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that, having regard to all the circumstances of the case (including those connected with his appointment), he ought fairly to be excused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1157(1) the court may relieve the defendant from liability` MEANS
    CONSIDER defendant
    WHEN `s 1157 another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against— (a) an officer of a company, or (b) a person employed by a company as auditor"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the proceedings are for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust`
           AND `it appears to the court that the defendant is or may be liable`
           AND `it appears to the court that the defendant acted honestly and reasonably`
           AND `it appears to the court that, having regard to all the circumstances of the case (including those connected with his appointment), he ought fairly to be excused`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If in proceedings for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust ... it appears to the court hearing the case that the officer or person is or may be liable but that he acted honestly and reasonably, and that having regard to all the circumstances of the case ... he ought fairly to be excused, the court may relieve him" (a grant of power whose "if" gate is unmet: fork F19)

-- src:16442 | (2) If any such officer or person has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against him in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust—
-- src:16443 | (a) he may apply to the court for relief, and
-- src:16444 | (b) the court has the same power to relieve him as it would have had if it had been a court before which proceedings against him for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust had been brought.
@ref s 1157(2) Application for relief by an officer or auditor who apprehends a claim (src:16442-16444)
GIVEN defendant IS A `s 1157 defendant`
      `he has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against him in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1157(2)(a) the person may apply to the court for relief` MEANS
    CONSIDER defendant
    WHEN `s 1157 another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such officer or person"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `he has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against him in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any such officer or person has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against him ... he may apply to the court for relief"

-- src:16442 | (2) If any such officer or person has reason to apprehend that a claim will or might be made against him in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust—
-- src:16443 | (a) he may apply to the court for relief, and
-- src:16444 | (b) the court has the same power to relieve him as it would have had if it had been a court before which proceedings against him for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust had been brought.
@ref s 1157(2) The court's power on such an application (src:16442-16444)
GIVEN `the person has applied to the court for relief under subsection (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1157(1) the court may relieve the defendant from liability` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1157(2)(b) the court has the same power to relieve the applicant` MEANS
    IF `the person has applied to the court for relief under subsection (2)(a)`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 1157(1) the court may relieve the defendant from liability`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court has the same power to relieve him as it would have had if it had been a court before which proceedings against him ... had been brought" (a JUST FALSE answer to s 1157(1) is passed through; s 1157(1) itself answers NOTHING when its "if" is unmet: fork F19)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 1157(1) answer is not known
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) he may apply to the court for relief, and (b) the court has the same power"

-- src:16445 | (3) Where a case to which subsection (1) applies is being tried by a judge with a jury, the judge, after hearing the evidence, may, if he is satisfied that the defendant (in Scotland, the defender) ought in pursuance of that subsection to be relieved either in whole or in part from the liability sought to be enforced against him, withdraw the case from the jury and forthwith direct judgment to be entered for the defendant (in Scotland, grant decree of absolvitor) on such terms as to costs (in Scotland, expenses) or otherwise as the judge may think proper.
@ref s 1157(3) A judge trying the case with a jury may withdraw it and direct judgment for the defendant (src:16445)
GIVEN `the case is one to which subsection (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is being tried by a judge with a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge, after hearing the evidence, is satisfied that the defendant ought to be relieved in whole or in part from the liability sought to be enforced against him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1157(3) the judge may withdraw the case from the jury and direct judgment for the defendant` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the case is one to which subsection (1) applies` AND `the case is being tried by a judge with a jury`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a case to which subsection (1) applies is being tried by a judge with a jury" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    ELSE IF `the judge, after hearing the evidence, is satisfied that the defendant ought to be relieved in whole or in part from the liability sought to be enforced against him`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the judge, after hearing the evidence, may, if he is satisfied that the defendant ... ought ... to be relieved either in whole or in part" (a grant of power whose "if" gate is unmet: fork F27)
